<title>USA: Ameriana to buy back up to 300,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Ameriana to buy back up to 300,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW CASTLE, Ind. 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ameriana Bancorp, a $402.2 million-asset bank holding company, said Thursday its directors had authorized the repurchase of up to 300,000 of its 3.3 million outstanding common shares.</p>
<p>Directors have authorized the expenditure of up to $5 million for the repurchases.</p>
<p>The authorization expires in June 1998.  </p>
<p>Ameriana said the buyback will depend on market conditions. Share repurchases will be made in the open market or in negotiated transactions.</p>
<p>Under a repurchase program that expires this month, Ameriana had bought back 127,966 shares at a total cost of $1.9 million.</p>
<p>Shares of Ameriana were up 1-1/8 to 16-3/4.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
